# Test-config reference templates

## Template source

`tester-v1/test-configs/reference/reference-model/` is canonical. The create-new-model-test skill copies from here only — never from `test1/qwen3.5-9b-q8/` or other live model dirs.

## Keep reference updated

When you:

- Add, remove, or rename a variant directory under any real `test-configs/{suite}/{model}/`
- Change shared server.yaml / client.yaml structure, args, or default prompts intended for all new models
- Update the variant table in the create-new-model-test skill

Apply the same change under `reference/reference-model/` (and update the skill variant table if variants changed). Prefer editing reference first, then real models if the user asks.

## Do not run on reference

Do not run `python_runner.py` or `model_calibration.py` on paths under `test-configs/reference/`.

## Fixed directory name

`reference-model` is a fixed directory name; do not rename it to a real model slug.
